---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteNav from '../../components/SiteNav.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import { SITE_NAME } from '../../lib/events';

const title = `Privacy — ${SITE_NAME}`;
const description = `What ${SITE_NAME} collects, what it doesn't, and why.`;
---

<Base title={title} description={description} path="/privacy/">
	<SiteNav />

	<main class="wrap legal">
		<h1>Privacy</h1>
		<p class="intro">
			Short version: no cookies, no tracking across sites, no selling of anything. Here is the
			whole picture, as required by the Swiss Federal Act on Data Protection (FADP).
		</p>

		<h2>Who is responsible</h2>
		<p>
			Marcin Czajkowski, Geneva, Switzerland — <a href="mailto:czajkowski81@gmail.com"
				>czajkowski81@gmail.com</a
			>. See the <a href="/impressum/">Impressum</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Just browsing</h2>
		<p>
			The site is static and sets no cookies. Visits are counted with Cloudflare Web Analytics,
			which is cookie-free and does not build a profile of you: it records aggregate page views,
			referrers, country and browser type, without storing your IP address. The site's typeface
			is loaded from Google Fonts, so your browser requests the font files from Google's servers;
			Google may record the request under its own privacy policy. Hosting is on GitHub Pages
			(GitHub, Inc., USA), which keeps standard server logs.
		</p>

		<h2>Links to organisers</h2>
		<p>
			Registration buttons link to the organiser's own page and carry a tag
			(<code>utm_source=swissdataevents.ch</code>) so organisers can see that a visitor came from
			here. Nothing about you is sent — only that this site was the referrer. What the organiser's
			page does with your data is governed by their privacy policy, not this one.
		</p>

		<h2>The weekly digest</h2>
		<p>
			If you subscribe, your email address is used for one thing: sending you the weekly digest of
			new Swiss data and AI events. It is never sold, shared or added to anything else. Unsubscribe
			at any time via the link in every email or by writing to the address above, and it is
			deleted.
		</p>

		<h2>Contact and event-submission forms</h2>
		<p>
			Forms are relayed by FormSubmit (formsubmit.co), which forwards what you typed to the inbox
			above and keeps nothing beyond what it needs to deliver the message. Your details are used
			only to reply to you or to list the event you submitted. Organiser names on event listings
			are public information taken from the organiser's own page.
		</p>

		<h2>Your rights</h2>
		<p>
			You can ask what is held about you, have it corrected or deleted, at any time — one email is
			enough. If sponsorships or paid listings are ever introduced, this page will be updated first.
		</p>

		<p class="updated">Last updated 5 September 2026.</p>
	</main>

	<SiteFooter />

	<style>
		.legal {
			padding: 24px 32px 64px;
			max-width: 640px;
		}
		h1 {
			font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2rem);
			margin: 16px 0 8px;
			letter-spacing: -0.01em;
		}
		h2 {
			font-size: 0.95rem;
			font-weight: 600;
			margin: 28px 0 6px;
		}
		p {
			margin: 0;
			line-height: 1.65;
			color: var(--ink-2);
		}
		.intro {
			color: var(--muted);
		}
		code {
			font-size: 0.85em;
			background: var(--chip-bg);
			padding: 1px 5px;
		}
		.updated {
			margin-top: 36px;
			font-size: 0.82rem;
			color: var(--muted);
		}
		@media (max-width: 640px) {
			.legal {
				padding: 16px 18px 48px;
			}
		}
	</style>
</Base>
